fo (bool): whether the agent received pro-mask information/exposure that day (event flag, not cumulative).\n\n- Relationships:\n  - Grouping by agent_id yields a longitudinal sequence of states over days.\n  - Temporal dependence is implied: wearing_mask at day t may depend on wearing_mask at t−1 and received_info at t or t−1 (design choice).\n  - No explicit social network structure is present; “received_info” likely represents the outcome of information transmission (from neighbors or exogenous sources), but edges/exposures are not included here.\n\n- How this informs simulation entities/interactions:\n  - Initialize agents: each agent has state variables wearing_mask (bool) and optionally an info buffer (e.g., received_info_today, exposures_count).\n  - Calibrate behavior dynamics from this training data:\n    - Estimate transition probabilities P(wearing_t | wearing_t−1, received_info_{t or t−1}) and relapse rates P(unwear_t | wear_{t−1}, no_info).\n    - Decide same-day vs lagged effect of received_info based on best empirical fit.\n  - Drive interactions: in the simulation, received_info should be generated via the social network (e.g., from masked neighbors, influencers, campaigns); use calibrated transition rules to update wearing_mask.\n  - Missing components to source/generate:\n    - Network topology (edges, influence weights).\n    - Exogenous info processes (broadcasts) if needed to match observed received_info rates.\n  - Data handling notes:\n    - Ensure booleans are parsed from CSV correctly (often as strings).\n    - Check for complete day ranges per agent, duplicates, and monotonic day ordering.\n\nCALIBRATION CONTEXT:\n{\n  "task_description": "Develop a multi-agent simulation system that models the spread of mask-wearing behavior through social networks.",\n  "metrics": [\n    {\n      "name": "\\u603b\\u4f53\\u91c7\\u7eb3\\u7387\\u968f\\u65f6\\u95f4",\n      "description": "\\u6bcf\\u4e2a\\u65f6\\u95f4\\u6b65\\u5168\\u4f53\\u4eba\\u53e3\\u7684\