ool): agent\\u2019s mask-wearing state on that day (point-in-time, not cumulative).\\n  - received_info (bool): whether the agent received pro-mask information/exposure that day (event flag, not cumulative).\\n\\n- Relationships:\\n  - Grouping by agent_id yields a longitudinal sequence of states over days.\\n  - Temporal dependence is implied: wearing_mask at day t may depend on wearing_mask at t\\u22121 and received_info at t or t\\u22121 (design choice).\\n  - No explicit social network structure is present; \\u201creceived_info\\u201d likely represents the outcome of information transmission (from neighbors or exogenous sources), but edges/exposures are not included here.\\n\\n- How this informs simulation entities/interactions:\\n  - Initialize agents: each agent has state variables wearing_mask (bool) and optionally an info buffer (e.g., received_info_today, exposures_count).\\n  - Calibrate behavior dynamics from this training data:\\n    - Estimate transition probabilities P(wearing_t | wearing_t\\u22121, received_info_{t or t\\u22121}) and relapse rates P(unwear_t | wear_{t\\u22121}, no_info).\\n    - Decide same-day vs lagged effect of received_info based on best empirical fit.\\n  - Drive interactions: in the simulation, received_info should be generated via the social network (e.g., from masked neighbors, influencers, campaigns); use calibrated transition rules to update wearing_mask.\\n  - Missing components to source/generate:\\n    - Network topology (edges, influence weights).\\n    - Exogenous info processes (broadcasts) if needed to match observed received_info rates.\\n  - Data handling notes:\\n    - Ensure booleans are parsed from CSV correctly (often as strings).\\n    - Check for complete day ranges per agent, duplicates, and monotonic day ordering."\n  ]\n}\n\nPlease design a simulation model that addresses the task requirements. Your response should include:\n\n1. The most appropriate modeling approach (agent-based, system dynamics, network-based, etc.)\n2. The structure of the simulation (entities, behaviors, interactions)\n3. The environment representation (grid, continuous space, network, etc.)\n4. Necessary parameters and configuration options\n5. Initialization procedures\n6. The algorithms to implement key behaviors and interactions\n7. A plan for how the code should be structured\n8. Any prediction or evaluation period specified by the task (e.g., days 30-39), and include it as a `prediction_period` field in the model plan.\n9. The evaluation metrics required by the task, and include them as an `evaluation_metrics` list in the model plan.\n\nResponse Format:\nPlease structure your response as a JSON object with the following structure:\n{\n  "model_type": "agent_based | system_dynamics | network | etc.",\n  "description": "Brief description of the model approach",\n  "entities": [\n    {\n      "name": "Entity name",\n      "attributes": ["attribute1", "attribute2", ...],\n      "behaviors": ["behavior1", "behavior2", ...],\n      "initialization": {\n        "method": "random | data_driven | specified",\n        "parameters": { ... }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  "behaviors": [\n    {\n      "name": "behavior_name",\n      "description": "Description of the behavior",\n      "applicable_to": ["Entity1", "Entity2", ...],\n      "parameters": { ... },\n      "algorithm": "Description of algorithm or approach"\n    }\n  ],\n  "interactions": [\n    {\n      "name": "interaction_name",\n      "description": "Description of the interaction",\n      "entities_involved": ["Entity1", "Entity2", ...],\n      "trigger": "proximity | time | state | etc.",\n      "effect": "Description of the effect"\n    }\n  ],\n  "environment": {\n    "type": "grid | continuous | network | etc.",\n    "dimensions": [x, y] or null,\n    "time_step": value,\n    "time_unit": "seconds | minutes | hours | days | etc."\n  },\n  "parameters": {\n    "param1": value1,\n    "param2": value2,\n    ...\n  },\n  "initialization": {\n  